{"season":2026,"week":11,"kind":"preview","league":"67FFL","my_team":"ATX Bowers","generated_utc":"2026-11-19T22:49Z","writer":"claude","headline":"Week 11: Kincaid's thumb, the trade deadline, and small upgrades","dek":"ATX Bowers projects at 117.9 points, and a few free-agent swaps are worth about 2.8 more.","sections":[{"id":"my_lineup","title":"Your best lineup","md":"Our projection has ATX Bowers at **117.9** points this week. That is 8th of 12 teams by projected starting points. The Dakstreet Boys lead at 131.2.\n\n**Best lineup:**\n- QB: Bo Nix (18.13)\n- RB: Tony Pollard (18.66), Jonah Coleman (13.88)\n- WR: Rashee Rice (11.42), Deebo Samuel Sr. (10.85)\n- TE: Dalton Kincaid (9.03)\n- FLEX: Aaron Jones (10.59), Tank Dell (9.07)\n- K: Wil Lutz (8.40)\n- DEF: NYJ D/ST (7.87)\n\n**Out of play:**\n- Drake Maye is listed Out and flagged as being on a bye, so Nix is the QB.\n- Denzel Boston is also on a bye.\n\n**Injury watch:**\n- Kincaid did not practice (DNP, thumb). He is the one to check before kickoff. Brenton Strange (8.92) is the fallback, and the gap between them is only 0.11 (see Close calls).\n- Rice (knee) and Dell (hand) both practiced fully.\n\nThree starters are Broncos: Nix, Coleman and Lutz. Their outcomes will move together this week."},{"id":"close_calls","title":"Close calls","md":"**TE: Dalton Kincaid (9.03) over Brenton Strange (8.92), margin 0.11.**\n\nThis is a coin flip on paper, but the pre-game signals lean Kincaid:\n- **Production:** 10.3 PPR per game this season and 10.7 over the last three, against 8.9 and 6.9 for Strange.\n- **Expected points:** xFP over the last three games is 7.7 for Kincaid and 5.0 for Strange.\n- **Vegas:** BUF is implied at 30.5 against MIA. JAX is implied at 26.2 against NYG.\n- **Against Kincaid:** his snap share has slid from 62% on the season to 51% over the last three. Strange sits at 76% and 70%. Kincaid also did not practice, which is the real risk.\n\nIf Kincaid is out or limited, Strange is the move. A better answer may be Dalton Schultz on waivers (see below)."},{"id":"waivers","title":"Waiver adds and streamers","md":"These are the free agents who beat or match someone in my lineup. Our projection gives a total gain of about **2.8 points** if all four swaps happen.\n\n**TE: Dalton Schultz, HOU (9.80).**\n- That is +0.77 over Kincaid.\n- HOU is implied at 28.5 against IND.\n- Schultz also covers the Kincaid thumb risk.\n- His snap share is 57% and his target share over the last three is 13%.\n\n**WR: Adonai Mitchell, NYJ (9.97).**\n- He is +0.90 over Dell in the FLEX spot.\n- The underlying usage is stronger than the projection: 24% target share and 79% of snaps over the last three, with xFP of 16.6.\n- The caution is that NYJ is implied at only 19.2.\n\n**K: Tyler Bass, BUF (9.24).** That is +0.84 over Lutz. Harrison Butker (8.84) is also ahead of Lutz.\n\n**DEF: LAC D/ST or JAX D/ST (8.20 each).** That is +0.33 over NYJ D/ST. It is a small gain, and only worth it if the roster spot is free.\n\n**Other names:**\n- Makai Lemon, PHI WR (8.81): 27% target share and 93% of snaps over the last three. PHI is implied at just 16.5, though, and Joe Milton III has one game of data.\n- Cam Ward, TEN QB (16.15): he trails Nix at 18.13, so he is not an upgrade.\n- Bryce Young, CAR QB (16.25): same story as Ward."},{"id":"buy_sell","title":"Buy low, sell high","md":"The trade deadline is this week (week 11), so any move has to happen now. These numbers compare PPR per game to xFP per game on my own roster.\n\n**Sell high:**\n- **Deebo Samuel Sr.:** 14.4 PPR per game against 8.6 xFP, a gap of **+5.7**. He has scored well above what his usage predicts. Our projection has him at 10.85, which is already well below his scoring average.\n- **Rashee Rice:** 13.2 against 10.4, a gap of **+2.9**. This one is milder, and his usage is still solid.\n\nBoth are in my starting lineup, and WR is a need for this roster (31.3 strength against a league median of 38.4). Selling either only makes sense if the return is a WR who produces similar usage at a lower price.\n\n**Buy low (hold):**\n- **Bo Nix:** 14.5 PPR per game against 16.9 xFP, a gap of **-2.3**. He should be producing more than he has. He is my starter with Maye out, so the call is to hold.\n- **Jordan Addison:** 7.7 against 9.0, a gap of **-1.3**. He is a modest hold."},{"id":"around_league","title":"Around the league: needs and trade fits","md":"The trade-fit tool found no matches with my roster, so these are ideas to look at before the week 11 deadline, not recommendations.\n\n**My needs:** WR and TE. My RB group is a strength (43.1 against a league median of 33.8), and Brenton Strange is a surplus TE. The facts show no spare RB beyond my starters, so any RB deal would cost lineup points.\n\n**Ideas worth a look:**\n- **Just Win Baby (8-2):** WR is a strength (50.8), RB is a need (27.5), and they have no listed surplus. This is the cleanest WR-for-RB shape on paper. RJ Harvey is on their IR.\n- **The Dakstreet Boys (3-7):** WR is 51.5, RB is a need at 28.0, and they have Tre Tucker (8.40) as surplus. Tucker is not much of an upgrade for me, so the deal would be about their other WRs.\n- **I Love it Ra (6-4):** they have no needs and three surplus pieces: TE Chig Okonkwo (10.49), WR Josh Downs (9.88) and WR Antonio Williams (9.21). Okonkwo projects above Kincaid, and either WR would fit my need. They have nothing to gain at RB, though, so I would have to find something else they want.\n\n**Other teams, for context:**\n- Chentudo El Venudo (8-2) and Moore Than A Bite (7-3) both need a TE, so they are competing with me for the same position.\n- Game of Throws needs a QB, WR and TE but has a strong RB group (64.7)."}],"links":{"Bo Nix":"p:00-0039732","Tony Pollard":"p:00-0035261","Jonah Coleman":"p:00-0041496","Rashee Rice":"p:00-0039067","Deebo Samuel Sr.":"p:00-0035719","Dalton Kincaid":"p:00-0038933","Wil Lutz":"p:00-0032569","NYJ D/ST":"d:NYJ","Aaron Jones":"p:00-0033293","Tank Dell":"p:00